// LLAMP-SPEC v1 | ADR-039
=adr: 039
=title: dashboard-derived-state-endpoint
=date: 2026-03-02
=status: accepted

#ctx
~dashboard gauge blocks call GET /devices/:deviceId/states/latest via useDeviceRealtime
~that endpoint queries device_states (time-series, append-only raw telemetry) — ADR-031
~workflow-computed canonical snapshot lives exclusively in device_derived_states
  (one doc per device, upserted by writeDeviceState action, stale+staledAt from ADR-034)
~time-series query may return a raw telemetry record with no derived fields;
  gauges show incorrect or missing computed values on hard refresh / before WebSocket fires
~no dedicated HTTP endpoint exposes device_derived_states today

#opts
A. keep /states/latest, merge derived inline → N-query join, defeats collection separation
B. add GET /devices/:deviceId/derived-state backed by deviceDerivedStateService.getLatest()
   → clean single-responsibility; time-series stays for history only

#decision
=chosen: B
~add GET /devices/:deviceId/derived-state → deviceDerivedStateService.getLatest()
  response: { deviceId, derived:{}, lastSeen, stale, staledAt }
~useDeviceRealtime initial HTTP fetch switches from /states/latest → /derived-state
~device_states (time-series) = history/charts/exports ONLY — never used for live snapshot
~WebSocket live updates unchanged (already carry derived in payload)
~useDeviceFields reads device.derivedState from GET /devices/:deviceId — no change

#consequences
+clean separation: time-series→history, derived-state→live snapshot
+stale/staledAt propagated correctly on every hard refresh (no WebSocket dependency)
~useDeviceRealtime response shape changes: adapt DeviceState-compatible cache object
  data = derived (all workflow fields); derived = derived; timestamp = lastSeen
~/states/latest remains for other consumers (audit, raw data views) — not removed
!breaking: useDeviceRealtime callers must not assume data contains raw sensor fields
  (raw sensor fields remain in WebSocket payload — gauges still update in realtime)

#scope
=arch_summary_update: yes
=new_endpoint: GET /devices/:deviceId/derived-state
=affected: [device-state.controller, device-state.routes, useDeviceRealtime]
=task_type_split: backend→@sonnet | frontend→@haiku
